From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6asm-dai: keep the DSP buffer address inside 32 bits

q6asm-dai hands the DSP the buffer address with the low four bits of the
SMMU stream id in bits 32 and up:

	pdata->sid = args.args[0] & SID_MASK_DEFAULT;
	prtd->phys = substream->dma_buffer.addr | (pdata->sid << 32);

which only works if the mapping itself fits in 32 bits. With a 64 bit DMA
mask the iommu allocates from the top of the address space instead
(0x1_fff80000 was observed on SM6375), bit 32 is already set, and the
address the DSP receives is the two things overlapping rather than either
of them.

Downstream avoids this by confining the audio iova pool to a low window
("qcom,iommu-dma-addr-pool = <0x10000000 0x10000000>" on
qcom,msm-audio-ion). Asking for a 32 bit DMA mask achieves the same thing.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c	2026-08-12 17:59:35.043296011 +0000
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c	2026-08-12 17:59:35.069296011 +0000
@@ -1309,11 +1309,29 @@
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	rc = of_parse_phandle_with_fixed_args(node, "iommus", 1, 0, &args);
-	if (rc < 0)
+	if (rc < 0) {
 		pdata->sid = -1;
-	else
+	} else {
 		pdata->sid = args.args[0] & SID_MASK_DEFAULT;
 
+		/*
+		 * The address handed to the DSP is the buffer address with the
+		 * stream id in bits 32 and up (see prtd->phys below), so the
+		 * mapping itself has to fit in 32 bits or the two overlap and
+		 * the DSP is given an address that does not exist. Downstream
+		 * gets this by confining the audio iova pool to a low window
+		 * ("qcom,iommu-dma-addr-pool = <0x10000000 0x10000000>" on
+		 * qcom,msm-audio-ion); here it is enough to ask for a 32 bit
+		 * DMA mask, otherwise the iommu allocates from the top of the
+		 * 64 bit space (0x1_fff80000 was observed) and bit 32 is
+		 * already taken.
+		 */
+		rc = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+		if (rc)
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, rc,
+					     "cannot set 32 bit DMA mask\n");
+	}
+
 	dev_set_drvdata(dev, pdata);
 
 	rc = of_q6asm_parse_dai_data(dev, pdata);
